From: David Igou <igou.david@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: rockchip: allocate v2 page tables below 4 GiB

The IOMMU v2 hardware in RK35xx SoCs (rk3568-iommu compatible, also
used by the RK3588 NPU/VPU MMUs) fetches its DTE/PT page tables with
32-bit physical addresses. On boards with more than 4 GiB of RAM the
unconstrained allocations can land above 4 GiB, and the IOMMU then
raises AXI bus errors when walking them (observed as rknpu job
submissions that never start, raw status 0xC0010000, on a 16 GiB
ROCK 5B; reproduced independently on RK3566 by the rknpu-module
project). Constrain v2 page-table allocations with GFP_DMA32 the same
way v1 already does.

--- a/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
@@ -1358,6 +1358,6 @@ static struct rk_iommu_ops iommu_data_ops_v2 = {
 	.pt_address = &rk_dte_pt_address_v2,
 	.mk_dtentries = &rk_mk_dte_v2,
 	.mk_ptentries = &rk_mk_pte_v2,
 	.dma_bit_mask = DMA_BIT_MASK(40),
-	.gfp_flags = 0,
+	.gfp_flags = GFP_DMA32,
 };
